// Codex round 26 on ddd01cc2 (WIS-625 post-merge).
//   - The coordinate bound does not stop float32 underflow or drift: a 1e-10 scale flushes to
//     zero in float32, and a thousand 0.001 moves at x 99000 are lost in float32 (its step there is
//     0.0078) while float64 keeps them. A CTM whose area scale is below 1e-6 is refused; the CTM is
//     also computed in float32, and the glyph pass is run again in float32: any underflow, or a
//     glyph or box more than 0.01 unit apart, refuses the file.
//   - q, Q and cm inside BT ... ET: one reader keeps the text matrices across Q, another does not.
//     They, and paths, XObjects and inline images, are refused inside a text object.
//   - Blended text wholly off the page counted as blending on an isolated page.
//   - A blended image at alpha 0 counted as covering, and as blending.
